wolf> :help
:type e            evaluate e, report its type
:mem               the memory model, live: regions, loans, shared, pools, tasks
:regions           the region tree alone
:trace on|off      record rule firings (clause-cited) into the ring buffer
:trace show [n]    show the last n recorded events (default 20)
:trace clear       empty the ring buffer
:rules [prefix]    the rule registry, optionally filtered by anchor prefix
:schedule seed     re-seed the scheduler's decision stream from here on
:load file.lu      textual inclusion into the implicit module ([repl.module])
:reset             fresh world, empty module
:quit              leave
wolf> :rules conc.deadlock
[conc.deadlock.def] DeadlockDef: every live task blocked at a blocking point with no pending timer and no in-flight I/O is a deadlock — a defined outcome, detected exactly by a deterministic scheduler
[conc.deadlock.trap] DeadlockTrap: a detected deadlock terminates with trap kind `deadlock`, reporting the blocked-task roster; detection is required in deterministic test modes
[conc.deadlock.self] DeadlockSelf: acquiring a sync object the acquiring task already holds can never complete: detected immediately, `trap(deadlock)`
wolf> :type 1 < 2
bool
